500	76,1121,388,1678	500. Endogenous stem of one year old, shown in a Corn-stalk.	A short length of corn-stalk cut off slantwise at the top, the cut face dotted with scattered threads of wood in the pith and the sides finely lined.
501	67,700,500,1051	501. One of several years old, of Palmetto.	A thick piece of Palmetto trunk cut across, the broad top face crowded with countless small dots of wood bundles within a rough outer rind.
502	527,806,972,1676	Parallel-veined leaves of the two kinds: 502. that of Lily of the Valley;	A long oval pointed leaf whose many fine veins run side by side from the base to the tip without branching.
503	1008,816,1432,1667	503. one of Calla	A broad heart-shaped leaf with a strong midrib, from which many curved parallel veins run out towards the margin.
504	1459,712,1670,997	504. Magnified section of the seed of Iris, showing the small monocotyledonous embryo.	A rounded triangular seed cut through, its thick coat enclosing finely dotted albumen, with the small straight embryo near one corner.
